# Strings

Every user-visible string (labels, buttons, empty states, errors, content descriptions) must come from `app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`.

## Rules

- In Compose: `stringResource(R.string.*)` / `pluralStringResource`.
- Never hardcode UI copy in Kotlin (`"Search"`, `"Home"`, etc.).
- Add a new `<string>` (or plurals) when introducing copy; reuse existing keys when meaning matches.
- Keep keys descriptive: `nav_*`, `action_*`, `home_*`, `search_*`, `settings_*`, `media_*`, `error_*`.
- Format args with `%1$s` / `%1$d` — do not concatenate translated sentences in code.
- Content descriptions for icons/controls also use string resources.
- Debug-only / preview placeholders may use string resources too (see `greeting_*`).
